Results (details in render-measurements.log)
- Page overflow: false on all 15 page/viewport combinations. No element wider
  than the viewport anywhere.
- Headings: no skipped levels on any page (h1 -> h2 -> h3 only).
- Images: every visible figure image loaded with descriptive alt text matching
  the figure manifest; the only unloaded images are the .figure__img--dark
  variants, which are display:none in light theme by design (Spec 013 dual
  variant) and load on theme switch. Print forces the light variant; figure
  break-inside: avoid confirmed.
- Tables: all content tables fit at every viewport (scrollWidth === clientWidth)
  except the teacher-notes sequencing table at 360px (scrollWidth 363 inside
  clientWidth 328): it is its own scroll container, its last column right edge
  comes from 379 (past the 360px viewport) to 344 after scrolling (reachable),
  and hydration added tabindex="0", role="region", aria-label="Scrollable
  table, scroll sideways to see all columns". Tables that fit carry no tabindex,
  which is the intended conditional behaviour (src/theme/DocItem/Content.tsx).
- Print: navbar and .theme-doc-sidebar-container hidden, body width 794, no
  clipping of figures or the answers section (no overflow, no wide elements).
- Badge and print-handout elements render on all five pages.

Limitation
- In-session viewing of the saved PNGs was blocked by this environment (Read on
  PNG returns no image), as in prior review rounds. PNG validity and
  non-blankness were verified programmatically (png-stats.log, sharp channel
  stdev 43.9-61.2); the substantive accessibility checks above are the logged
  DOM-level measurements, which are stronger evidence than visual impression.

Verdict for the accessibility criterion: PASS at all three viewports.
